            <chunk name="Object" index="3">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">df79d86f-35e0-5006-ae1a-ca2912e02b49</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: An annual wind rose for a city in the Rhino viewport.
Fidelity: Screening - bins the weather file as recorded; no simulation.
Method: Wind Compass bins every hour into 16 sectors stacked by speed; hours below 0.5 m/s count as calm.
Result: Petals sized by frequency and coloured by wind-speed band; the banner reports the hours plotted.
Needs: Nothing to install; Download Weather needs internet. Runtime: seconds.
Edit: Station panel, Radius, Base Point; insert a Weather component before Wind Compass, which rejects the file path.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="5">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>119</X>
                          <Y>156</Y>
                          <W>420</W>
                          <H>250</H>
